gBJ(){return"These use the weather type the provider gives for that hour, with its strength: light, plain or heavy rain, snow, drizzle and so on. A block (morning, noon, afternoon, evening, night) shows its most significant weather, so one hour of thunder makes it a thunder block. In daytime, an hour is lifted to a sunnier sky when the provider's own sunshine forecast for it is high (clear from 90 percent of the hour, mostly sunny from 70, partly cloudy from 40), because thin high cloud can make a cloud-based weather type look greyer than the sky really is. It is never made gloomier."},
